 "notes_for_editor": "NRHP nomination PDF is not digitised, so the chronology rests on Lighthouse Friends and Terry Pepper (both secondary, copyrighted; own words used, one short quotation each). Their Lighthouse Board and log-book material was not read in the original; the Lighthouse Board reports for 1850-1890 are not in the corpus. Sources disagree on: first year (1849/1850), fog-signal building (1930 Pepper and Land Trust; 1938 Lighthouse Friends), fog signal buildings (1874 engine house vs 1875 pair), reconstruction of signal apparatus (1890 vs 1899), automation (1953 Land Trust, 1978 Wikipedia lead; USLHS roster has Coast Guard crew to 1971), tower height (78 ft LHF vs 13 m record). Henry Corgan: 1924 Bulletin says entered service 1866 at Manitou; roster shows 1868-1873 as assistant. Hart's death account is James Corgan's log entry as quoted by Lighthouse Friends, based on assistant Gustafson's statement. Fog-signal hours: the 360-hour entry is from the report printed before fiscal 1894 in the same archive.org volume (probably fiscal 1893). 1934 Bulletin text is OCR. Roster lines through 1971 taken from the USLHS archive via roster.py; 'at least' spans are not appointments. Coast Guard-era names (1957-71) are as the archive prints them. Skipped: NRHP listing date, 1938 storm damage Bulletin (garbled OCR). Verifier 2026-10-27: Henry Corgan is Charles's brother per Pepper (not a son); Pepper's 1862 completion and 'few feet off' capsizing added as disagreements.",
